            "title": "Is Venezuela about to lose Citgo, its most prized foreign asset?",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "A U.S. court on Monday begins the final sale hearing of an auction of shares in the parent of Venezuela-owned refiner Citgo Petroleum to pay creditors, following heavy competition for the seventh largest U.S. refiner.  A court officer overseeing the auction in August changed his recommendation of winner to a $5.9 billion offer by an affiliate of hedge fund Elliott Investment Management, following a bidding war.  The change has triggered objections and intensified a fight between creditors and bondholders in pursuit of the same assets.",
